      <h2>About Princess Salme Spice Garden</h2>
      <div>Princess Salme Spice Garden in Kidichi honors Princess Salme (Emily Ruete, 1844–1924), a Zanzibari princess who fled to Germany and wrote 'Memoirs of an Arabian Princess,' offering a rare insider's view of 19th-century sultanate court life. The garden cultivates cloves, nutmeg, cinnamon, vanilla, cardamom, and black pepper in traditional plantation layout. Guided tours include spice tasting, traditional hand-grinding demonstrations, and storytelling about Princess Salme's remarkable life between two worlds. Optional Swahili lunch available.</div>
